From 1a7dd48fe6070398152bef90fc33630c839a9b65 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cruz <cruz@tbu.net>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 14:38:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 140/206] analyze_snapshot: thread data-region sizes through,
 but the guard is not live yet

Interrupted mid-round by a quota block; committing it because the
plumbing is real and it does not regress -- blobs still come out at
666708 on our Product .so.

What it does not do is close the bug it was filed for. SetDataSizes
defaults to 0 and is overridden only in MappedAppSnapshot, so on the ELF
path -- the one every fixture and every user actually takes -- region_size
arrives as 0 and DataRegionSize falls through to the unguarded read via
its own `region_size == 0 ||` escape.

Measured rather than reasoned: replacing that escape with `false` and
rebuilding drops --dump_blobs from 666708 to 463732, the pre-fix number.
The extra-block header is being read only because the bound is skipped.
So the bounds check is dead code on the path that needed it, and the
out-of-bounds read is exactly as unbounded as before.

The ELF loader does know its segment sizes -- it maps them -- so the
remaining work is exposing them, not inventing them. F19 stays open with
this recorded.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

